<title>UK: NWE jet steady as premums slip, gas oil firms.</title>
<headline>NWE jet steady as premums slip, gas oil firms.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE jet fuel was steady as a stronger IPE gas oil was counteracted by weaker premiums, traders said.</p>
<p>IPE November gas oil jumped by $5.25 to $240.75 per tonne, but jet cargo premiums slipped to around $36.00.</p>
<p>Speculation continued over whether cargoes from the Gulf could be arbitraged to Europe, after the customs duty paid for non-EC qualified origins.</p>
<p>-- Tom Ashby, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8145</p>
